  "problem_context": {
    "problem_statement": "Migrate exactly cmc_write_zeroes from C*/HOL to QCP/Rocq. Immutable source snapshot: /Users/nizitong/Documents/ChatGPT/Cmc/experiments/cmc_write_zeroes/baseline/cmc_concrete_emit_zeroes.c and .h. Shared source definitions/proofs: baseline/userlib/pure_lists.c, baseline/cmc_rep.c and baseline/userlib/array.c.\nPreserve the original runtime signature and body: int index=0; while(index != count) { data[cursor+index]=0; index=index+1; }. The original DOES NOT call cmc_write_byte; do not replace its direct store with a call.\nLogical parameter prefix:list Z. Precondition: 0<=cursor; 0<=count; cursor+count<=capacity; capacity<=2147483647; separating ownership of initialized unsigned-byte prefix data[0..cursor) with exact content prefix and uninitialized unsigned-byte suffix data[cursor..capacity). Postcondition: initialized prefix data[0..cursor+count) with exact content prefix ++ ireplicate(count,0), and uninitialized suffix data[cursor+count..capacity). Preserve zero count and zero capacity admissible cases, including cursor=count=capacity=0. Do not add full-array initialization, positive count, nonnull data for empty footprints, or extra upper bounds to simplify proof. Do not weaken the exact output list or residual ownership.\nThe previous byte case verified existing UCharArray::seg / UCharArray::undef_seg as suitable mappings, at QCP_examples/QCP_demos_human/cmc_write_byte_migration.c. Reuse existing QCP/Rocq repeat/zeros/list lemmas where semantically equivalent. Source ireplicate uses an integer count; inspect its definition and bridge nonnegative counts correctly to nat repeats. Keep any newly required common definitions and helper lemmas distinct from case annotation/proofs for separate effort accounting. If no new public models/lemmas are needed, report zero rather than duplicating existing libraries.\nThe QCP formal contract is to be authored by annotation owner from these source semantics (no existing frozen QCP text). Follow controller-owned role boundaries. No new Axiom or Admitted in handwritten manual or case lib; report existing QCP automatic trusted admissions explicitly. This case is a C* -> QCP migration, not whole CMC/TVM proof completion; do not use the deprecated arr_sum reverse experiment as a proof template. Preserve metrics and failures.",
